PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_7gateway_9platforms_10api_server_16APIServerAdapter_24_handle_chat_completions_2_on_tool_progress, "Send tool progress as a separate SSE event.\n\n                Previously, progress markers like ``\342\217\260 list`` were injected\n                directly into ``delta.content``.  OpenAI-compatible frontends\n                (Open WebUI, LobeChat, \342\200\246) store ``delta.content`` verbatim as\n                the assistant message and send it back on subsequent requests.\n                After enough turns the model learns to *emit* the markers as\n                plain text instead of issuing real tool calls \342\200\224 silently\n                hallucinating tool results.  See #6972.\n\n                The fix: push a tagged tuple ``(\"__tool_progress__\", payload)``\n                onto the stream queue.  The SSE writer emits it as a custom\n                ``event: hermes.tool.progress`` line that compliant frontends\n                can render for UX but will *not* persist into conversation\n                history.  Clients that don't understand the custom event type\n                silently ignore it per the SSE specification.\n                ");
